{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471096-green-bay-in-the-wod","id":1471096,"title":"Green Bay in the WoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-22T11:30:50-08:00","id":1471096,"title":"Green Bay in the WoD?","content":"Has anything been done with Green Bay in the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(I mean, everyone knows the Cheeseheads are a cover front for a combo of a Satanic group and the mafia. But that is in the real world. What about in the WoD?)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T19:59:09-08:00","id":1471120,"title":"","content":"Not that I am aware of, unless there is some small aside somewhere in Milwaukee by Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-22T22:12:16-08:00","id":1471124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471096-green-bay-in-the-wod?p=1471120#post1471120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I am aware of, unless there is some small aside somewhere in Milwaukee by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True.<br /> Though incidentally, based in a superficial reading of wiki sources, i think that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Hawk_(Sauk_leader)#War_of_1812\" target=\"_blank\">Chief Black Hawk</a>, who had a major part in the conflicts that served as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_of_1812\" target=\"_blank\">backdrop for Menele &amp; Helena's final fight before torpor</a>, led the native forces specifically from Green Bay.<br /> Also, a mysterious kindred known as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hrothulf\" target=\"_blank\">Petre Dubois</a> would strike occasional contact, some friendly, some not, with at least people of the Chippewa and Menominee tribes, from his arrival in the 1670s to the time of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Yaryan?so=search\" target=\"_blank\">Pale Wolf</a>'s fall in the 1810s (or 1830s, kind of sketchy that part).<br /> <br /> Thought it was all kind of worth mentioning for reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-23-2021, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T09:00:45-08:00","id":1471147,"title":"","content":"It's not important, I was just curious. I'm revising my book <i>Hunger from Beyond</i>, part of which involves the north end of Lake Michigan. I was looking at the map and wondering. That said it does mean the city is a proverbial blank slate for a campaign, and it is in the same larger region as Chicago, Milwaukee, Detriot and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T10:15:44-08:00","id":1471152,"title":"","content":"The aura of faith around Lambeau Field probably drives vampires away. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T20:08:40-08:00","id":1471173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471096-green-bay-in-the-wod?p=1471152#post1471152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aura of faith around Lambeau Field probably drives vampires away. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Inquisition uses it as a base of operations. They pretend to be fans of the Packers and hide weapons in those foam hats made to look like cheese wedges.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T05:15:26-08:00","id":1471271,"title":"","content":"Yes. In a Chronicle about Milwaukee, Green Bay was a refuge for a group of Nosferatu fugitives, children of Parovich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-04T15:44:19-08:00","id":1471805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471096-green-bay-in-the-wod?p=1471271#post1471271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. In a Chronicle about Milwaukee, Green Bay was a refuge for a group of Nosferatu fugitives, children of Parovich.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my own Milwaukee Chronicle, the childer of Parovich along with some Caitiffs (and Milo) formed an anarch gang called the Orlocks, with some stealth council support from Edward &amp; Jason, who are both quite distrusting of Parovich, and Lucina, who's experimenting with them and a few other groups as a way to dilute the numbers and power of the Night Children (ditched the Blood Brothers name to avoid confusion) and the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-04-2022, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}